# Rust Development Rules

## Code Style
- Follow Rust idioms and best practices
- Use idiomatic error handling with Result<T, E> and Option<T>
- Prefer using iterators and functional patterns over imperative loops
- Use descriptive variable names following snake_case convention
- Follow the Rust API guidelines

## Code Quality
- Avoid unwrap() and expect() in production code; handle errors properly
- Use clippy suggestions to improve code quality
- Keep functions focused and small
- Prefer composition over complex inheritance patterns
- Use cargo fmt for consistent formatting

## Documentation
- Add doc comments (///) for public APIs
- Include examples in doc comments where helpful
- Document safety requirements for unsafe code

## Testing
- Write unit tests in the same file using #[cfg(test)] modules
- Use descriptive test names that explain what is being tested
- Prefer integration tests for testing public APIs